## Why This Is Asked
Assesses hands-on windowed aggregation, per-key state management, late-data handling, and correct offset commits in a beginner KCNA setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tumbling windows, per-key state, late data handling, TTL, idempotent emits, offset management.

## Code Example
```javascript
class WindowedAggSink {
  constructor(windowMs, latenessMs) {
    this.windowMs = windowMs;
    this.latenessMs = latenessMs;
    this.state = new Map(); // windowStart -> deviceId -> sum
  }
  onMessage(msg) {
    // msg: { deviceId, value, timestamp, offset }
    const ws = this.windowStartFor(msg.timestamp);
    const bucket = (this.state.get(ws) = this.state.get(ws) || new Map());
    bucket.set(msg.deviceId, (bucket.get(msg.deviceId) || 0) + msg.value);
  }
  onWindowBoundary(now) {
    // emit and clean up windows that ended before now - latenessMx
  }
  commitOffsets() {
    // persist offsets after successful emits
  }
  getTotals() {
    // return current in-memory totals for inspection
  }
  windowStartFor(ts) {
    return Math.floor(ts / this.windowMs) * this.windowMs;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests the ability to design robust per-topic schema validation with proper error handling and reliable offset management in Kafka consumer applications.

## Key Concepts
- JSON schema validation with type checking for required fields
- Per-topic dead-letter queue (DLQ) implementation
- Offset commit semantics with at-least-once delivery guarantees
- Idempotent message publishing and canary testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function validateUserEvent(rawMessage) {
  try {
    const payload = JSON.parse(rawMessage);
    if (typeof payload.userId === 'string' && 
        typeof payload.signupDate === 'string' && 
        typeof payload.metadata === 'object') {
      return { valid: true, payload };
    }
  } catch (error) {
    // Parsing error
  }
  return { valid: false, error: 'Invalid user event schema' };
}
```

## Testing Approach
Deploy canary with mixed valid/invalid messages to validate schema enforcement, DLQ routing, and offset commit behavior before full rollout.

